/// A function of a module whose *name* has two segments (`nest.lib`, the file `nest/lib.cml`): the
/// word that names its `twice` is `nest::lib::twice`, which is the reading that has to hold the
/// module's name as the whole path and the function as the last segment. Split at the first `::`
/// this is a function `lib::twice` of a module `nest`, which is not what the module is called.
export func twice(n: int) => int {
    return n + n
}